    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T03:07:44Z",
    "body": "Fact from #2031 (branch `issue/2031-rest-adaptive`): the rest Adaptive generator already holds its own entries to this rule, inside the motion crate (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive/rest/entry.rs`). A plunge is posted only where the stock as given (`RestStock`) proves the whole cutter footprint clear, plus a margin of 0.1 mm or four grid cells, asked of the polygon and of a conservative raster; what the operation's own passes cleared is never credited to a plunge. Pinned by `without_the_entry_guard_a_plunge_lands_on_material` (unit) and, against a simulated roughing pass, by the plunge law of `crates/motion/tests/rest_adaptive/sim.rs` (`read`).\n\nNot covered there, still this issue's: the Waterline / Offset rings / Zigzag rest passes of `rest2d::rest_pocket`, and the centre-cutting plunge law (`plunge_law`), which reads only what this path itself cleared and so treats a column an earlier operation cleared as solid.\n",
